<title>SWITZERLAND: ALPINE SKIING-ALPHAND WINS MEN'S WORLD CUP SUPER-G.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-ALPHAND WINS MEN'S WORLD CUP SUPER-G.</headline>
<dateline>LAAX, Switzerland 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Luc Alphand of France won a men's World Cup super-G race on Wednesday in a time of one minute 25.23 seconds, according to provisional results.  </p>
<p>Austria's Josef Strobl was second in 1:25.35 and Italian Peter Runggaldier finished third with a time of 1:25.63.</p>
